  "narrative": "I again use the signed-estimate convention: for direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means stronger measured dependency in the exposed group, i.e. a more negative raw dependency_composite; for direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means a higher/less-negative raw composite, i.e. weaker measured dependency. The central new result is that SMARCA4 loss was accepted and independently validated as a very large stronger-dependency association in TP53-loss-negative, KEAP1-loss-negative, MSI-negative cells. The highest-value next science is therefore not simply to test more binary predictors, but to determine whether the accepted marker effects are partly carried by SMARCA4 co-occurrence, whether SMARCA4 itself remains detectable in other marker backgrounds, and whether any residual threshold-level predictors remain in an accepted-marker-free and SMARCA4-intact stratum.\n\nI first register conditional independence checks for the accepted markers in SMARCA4-intact cells. TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are tested with the accepted weaker/higher-composite direction; MSI-high and PTEN loss are tested with the accepted stronger-dependency direction. These tests ask whether each effect remains above the 0.15-unit threshold when SMARCA4 loss is excluded from the eligible population. If they remain robust, the current accepted associations are largely independent of the newly validated SMARCA4 axis. If an accepted marker becomes subthreshold only after requiring SMARCA4 loss, that suggests the original effect was context-dependent or confounded with SMARCA4 co-loss, rather than a failure of the original broad association.\n\nI also register SMARCA4 context tests in TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, PTEN-loss, and MSI-high backgrounds. TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, and MSI-high have effects in the opposite direction from SMARCA4 loss or otherwise large dependencies, so SMARCA4 effects in those contexts may be attenuated by co-occurring effects; nevertheless, I hypothesize residual stronger-dependency signals from SMARCA4 loss. The PTEN-loss context tests whether two stronger-dependency predictors, SMARCA4 loss and PTEN loss, appear additive or concentrated in shared contexts. These are not causal claims about marker mechanisms; they are dataset-level tests of whether the SMARCA4 association persists across genetic backgrounds.\n\nThe CDKN2A reversal is refined. The previous conditional CDKN2A loss estimate was above the 0.15 threshold by point estimate but had a confidence interval extending below it, so the claim remains unresolved. I test CDKN2A loss again in a stricter clean stratum excluding TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, MSI-high, and SMARCA4 loss. The hypothesis is that CDKN2A loss still associates with stronger measured dependency. A threshold-level effect would strengthen the reversal; a null or subthreshold effect would make the CDKN2A claim much less compelling.\n\nFor broad exploration of additional measured predictors, I register BRCA2 loss and ERBB2 amplification in the same clean, SMARCA4-intact stratum. BRCA2 loss may mark DNA-repair deficiency, and ERBB2 amplification may mark oncogene-driven biology; both are plausible, falsifiable candidates for stronger dependency, so the expected raw contrast is negative and the claim direction is -1. These are dataset-level association hypotheses only. If they cross threshold, they become candidates for validation; if not, they can be deprioritized.\n\nFinally, I register one constructed-signature context test rather than relying on continuous main-effect contrasts whose analysis encoding would be uncertain. I test whether the SMARCA4-loss stronger-dependency effect is enhanced in cells with research_signature_a at or above one standardized unit. This is a direct test of whether a constructed signature modifies the strongest current context-specific association. The anticipated direction is stronger dependency in high-signature cells; a near-zero interaction would argue against this signature modifying SMARCA4 biology.\n\nI defer H44, the SMARCA4-by-lineage_subtype interaction, because the lineage_subtype main effect was rejected and the marker-specific main associations appear less obviously lineage-dependent than marker co-occurrence with SMARCA4. This frees analysis priority for independence checks, CDKN2A refinement, SMARCA4 context tests, and targeted predictor discovery. If analyze can only take a limited set, I would prioritize the accepted-marker independence checks, SMARCA4 main already registered, CDKN2A refinement, BRCA2/ERBB2 clean-stratum tests, and selected SMARCA4 context tests. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations unless independently validated, and none establish causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted supplied-dataset associations: MSI_high -> stronger dependency (-1), robust in TP53-intact, TP53/KEAP1-intact, Avana; TP53_loss -> weaker/higher composite (+1), robust in MSI-negative, KEAP1-intact, Avana; KEAP1_loss -> weaker/higher composite (+1 post-hoc reversal), robust in TP53-intact, TP53/MSI-clean, Avana, still no independent validation but very large precise discovery; PTEN_loss -> stronger dependency (-1), discovery +0.239, independent validation +0.294, moderate; PTEN_loss in KEAP1-intact -> stronger dependency, discovery +0.250, validation +0.240 with conservative lower bound below threshold, moderate conditional; SMARCA4_loss in TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative cells -> stronger dependency (-1), discovery +0.807 and independent validation +0.793, strongly supported conditional association. Negative/closed: lineage subtype main, KRAS, BRAF, MTAP, STK11 overall, MYC, EGFR original direction, markers D/E/F, STK11 in KEAP1-intact, RB1 in clean stratum, ARID1A in clean stratum, TP53-loss batch interaction, KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction, PTEN-by-PIK3CA original interaction direction. Unresolved/deferred: CDKN2A reversal H42 in clean stratum active (+0.168, CI +0.100 to +0.235); TP53/MSI interactions H29/H30 deferred due small MSI-positive overlap cells; lineage-specific accepted-marker checks H16-H18, PTEN in PIK3CA-wild-type H23 deferred/lower priority; SMARCA4-by-lineage H44 now deferred because lineage main null and higher-priority SMARCA4 independence/context tests are available. Active pending from last iteration: H43 SMARCA4 main overall; H45 PTEN loss in PIK3CA-mutant cells. New registered follow-ups: TP53_loss in KEAP1-intact/MSI-neg/SMARCA4-intact; KEAP1_loss in TP53-intact/MSI-neg/SMARCA4-intact; MSI_high in TP53-intact/KEAP1-intact/SMARCA4-intact; PTEN_loss in TP53/KEAP1/MSI/SMARCA4-intact; SMARCA4_loss within TP53-loss cells with KEAP1/MSI clean; SMARCA4_loss within KEAP1-loss cells with TP53/MSI clean; SMARCA4_loss within PTEN-loss cells with large markers clean; SMARCA4_loss within MSI_high cells; CDKN2A reversal in clean + SMARCA4-intact; BRCA2_loss and ERBB2_amplification in clean + SMARCA4-intact; SMARCA4-by-research_signature_a interaction. If analyze must select limited claims, prioritize accepted-marker independence from SMARCA4, SMARCA4 main, CDKN2A refinement, then new predictor clean-stratum tests and selected SMARCA4 context tests. Validation status: H8, H28, H40 have independent validation. Remaining validation slots may be useful later for KEAP1 main or a validated clean-context marker such as BRCA2/ERBB2 if threshold crossed. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations, not causal claims."
